Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1095)}Jaguar cubs stick with their\Nmothers for the first few years.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.30,0:00:14.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1095)}She weaned him six months ago,\Nbut he still counts on her to
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.72,0:00:16.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1095)}catch his dinner and keep him\Nsafe.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.04,0:00:33.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1095)}He's going to be bigger than she\Nis soon, but inside, he's still
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.52,0:00:34.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1095)}all cub.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.34,0:00:55.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1095)}They are 15 meters away, less\Nthan 50 feet, and they're so\Nrelaxed
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.52,0:00:58.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1095)}that I've managed to actually\Nget out the boat and sit here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.38,0:01:08.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1095)}There's the female there, and\Nthere's the cub just over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.20,0:01:19.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1095)}I'm just so grateful to them for\Ngiving us just a little window
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.62,0:01:21.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\pos(540,1095)}into the secret life of the\Ncubs.
